# regression-suite.sh generated artifacts (per-run, machine-specific)
# .selfcheck is harness-selfcheck.sh's scratch tree (kept only under KEEP=1);
# .guard-tmp holds one vector's captured oracle output while run.sh's harness
# guards inspect it. Both are deleted on a normal exit and are listed here so an
# interrupted run cannot leave a staged directory behind.
regression-suite/.selfcheck/
regression-suite/.guard-tmp/
# PID-scoped since 2026-08-21 (d4ca67040 made .guard-tmp concurrent-safe by
# renaming it to `.guard-tmp.$$`). The line above is anchored to the exact old
# name, so the rename ESCAPED it: every sweep began leaving an untracked
# directory, and a `git add -A` during a live run committed two of its oracle
# scratch files. `.jdk-only-reports.*` in regression-suite/.gitignore already
# had the pattern; this is the same convention, applied to the same shape.
regression-suite/.guard-tmp.*/
regression-suite/.mut/
test-infra/_regression-cratonvm-shim.bat
test-infra/suite-results/_cm-*.log
/target-gpu/
hs_err_pid*.log
build-wt.*
build-*.out
check-wt.*
build-*.log

# stray developer probe output
/dd1.out



# Merge-conflict side-copies of crate sources. Resolving a conflict in a file
# the size of native-builtins/src/lib.rs (~86k lines) tends to leave 3 MB
# `*.dev.rs` / `*.merge.rs` scratch copies at the repo root; two of them were
# committed and carried ~6.7 MB of dead duplicate source before being removed.
# They are never build inputs (no Cargo.toml or build.rs references them).
/*-lib.dev.rs
/*-lib.merge.rs
/*.dev.rs
/*.merge.rs
/*.merge.md

# Local-only vendored JDK reference checkout (used ad hoc against
# tools/flag-census/census.py, which explicitly skips this dir). Never a
# build input; one file slipped into tracking before this rule existed.
/jdk25src/

# Compiled/build output under spring-suite; sources (e.g. MRun.java) stay
# tracked, but .class/.out/.err build products should not be.
spring-suite/build/

# Personal / machine-specific dev build scripts (hardcoded usernames, dated
# worktree paths, one-off investigation output names). scripts/README.md has
# documented this as gitignored policy since before this rule actually
# existed in .gitignore; scripts/internal/ had been tracked in the meantime.
#scripts/internal/
#scripts/smoke/

# Generated by scripts/evidence/collect.{sh,ps1} — a run manifest, never committed.
/evidence/

# Compiled probe classes — `probes/*.java` sources stay tracked, their build
# output does not (the same rule `bench/` and `spring-suite/build/` already
# have; `probes/` itself is tracked, so it needs its own line).
probes/out/
# `VoxelAlloc2`'s nested classes compile to `VoxelAlloc2$*.class`, which the
# `probes/*.class` line below does not cover once they are put in their own
# output directory (the probe's doc comment uses `-d probes/voxout`).
probes/voxout/
# …including a probe compiled in place: the rule above only covers `out/`, so
# `javac probes/Foo.java` left a `probes/Foo.class` that `git add -A` tracked.
probes/*.class
# Same rule for the perf probes that live beside their harness under
# regression-suite/perf/: the .java sources are the artifact, the .class files
# a javac by-product.
regression-suite/perf/**/*.class

# local run artifacts
dim4-*.log*
build-win.log
cv-url.txt
hs-url.txt

# H2 corpus runs write their database here (regression-suite/corpus).
# Test output, not source.
data/
scratchpad/

# Raw frame dumps written by RayTracerKernel/RayTracerTornado's optional
# dumpPath argument and by bench-gpu/run-raytracer-comparison.sh. One
# 1920x1440 frame is 11 MB and a full sweep writes ~20 of them; they are
# regenerated by re-running the sweep and are never an input to anything.
bench-gpu/results/dumps/
